{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED — independent review of the dead-helper cleanup at exact head cd375dc3878efc9810f49dfb5b2f1160b1a2db67, artifact b09c3711 at internal/kernel, for review request 10f3c137 under request 8d0e995c.\n\nSCOPE. The diff against main d6843b48 is 8 deleted lines in internal/kernel/checkpoint.go and nothing else — no other file, no insertion. It removes exactly the two functions the request named: appendCheckpointEvent, which delegated to appendCheckpointEventInto, and validateCompactCheckpoint, which delegated to validateCompactCheckpointInto. Neither name occurs anywhere in the tree afterwards. No *Into implementation was edited, so this is removal of unreferenced code and carries no behaviour change.\n\nTHE FIVE RETAINED PAIRS ARE UNTOUCHED AND STILL LIVE. Counted across the whole package including tests at this exact head: loadCheckpoint 2 call sites, authenticateCheckpointCandidate 1, validateCheckpointEvents 1, scanListedAfter 3, newDeltaScan 1. None became dead as a consequence of this deletion, which was the risk worth checking.\n\nGATES, INDEPENDENTLY RUN. I cut my own worktree at the exact head. gofmt -l reports nothing, go build ./... exits 0, and go test -count=1 ./... passes 27 packages with zero failures, including internal/kernel at 199s and internal/docset at 60s. Because the change deletes unreferenced code, a green suite is the whole test: there is no seam to mutate, since the deleted functions had no caller whose behaviour could change.\n\nARCHITECTURE. internal/kernel only, and no contract moves. Both deleted functions were unexported and unreferenced, so nothing outside the package could observe them and no layer contract in docs/reference/architecture.md is affected. Preserved.\n\nSECURITY. No trust or authority boundary is touched. Verification, signature checking, checkpoint admission, dedup and bounds all live in the *Into implementations, which are byte-identical here. Deleting a delegating wrapper that nothing called cannot weaken a check, and cannot change which code runs. No defect.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. This head is itself the simplification I asked for in the approval of 052db91d, and it is exactly the size it should be: two functions, no opportunistic extras folded in. Condition 8 of request bc92fd60 asked that the stranded-predecessor repair stay out of this head, and it did. Nothing further to cut.\n\nONE NOTE, not a defect in this head and not a change request. Codex published two artifacts at internal/kernel for this commit and self-retired the first, da9410ba, leaving b09c3711 live and correct. That is the right repair and needs nothing. Separately, internal/kernel currently carries four live artifacts — this candidate b09c3711 at cd375dc3, the shipped successor f713bdb8 at merge d6843b48, the unmerged candidate 10937ebc at 9197c43b, and the stranded shipped predecessor 9736b0cd at c436808c. Only the last is a defect, it is not caused by this head, and it is already assigned as request bc92fd60. Whoever merges this head should retire the predecessor it supersedes at internal/kernel per AGENTS.md step 5, so this merge does not add a second stranded row on the same path.\n\nNo change to this head is required. Any change to it invalidates this approval.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b09c371110959be921d787875d2455278a29586c","head":"cd375dc3878efc9810f49dfb5b2f1160b1a2db67","verdict":"approved"}}